======================================================================================================================
L38 -- Type Ia supernovae re-examined for this framework: the a0(z) pipeline, SN-only, end to end
======================================================================================================================
  a0(z)/a0(0) = (1+z)^{1.5(1+w0+wa)} exp[-1.5 wa z/(1+z)]   -- EXACT closed form, never truncated
  footings: canonical (rho_Lambda) = 9.3619e-11 m s^-2 / alt (rho_total) = 1.1279e-10 m s^-2   (ratio 1.2048 = 1/sqrt(Omega_Lambda))
  host-mass-step lever: CLOSED (two null tests on the record); not re-opened anywhere below

