======================================================================================================================
B -- TARGET 1: does the REGISTERED 'flat 0.00 dex at z ~ 2.5' survive evolving dark energy?
======================================================================================================================
  the registered statistic (PAPER7, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22563139; STANDING.md; README):
    Delta_BTFR frozen against 0.00 dex (framework) and +0.33 dex (LCDM-native), one clean point at
    +/-0.13 dex, quoted as 20:1 discrimination.

  B1 -- SIGN CONVENTION.  In deep MOND V_f^4 = G a0 M_b exactly, so a change in a0 moves the zero
        point.  Two conventions are in circulation and PAPER7 uses BOTH, in the same paragraph:
  mass-side   Delta = log10 M_b - 4 log10 V_f - C0 = -log10[scale(z)/scale(0)]  ->  framework +0.085,  LCDM-native -0.328
  vel.-side   Delta = 4 log10 V_f - log10 M_b - C0' = +log10[scale(z)/scale(0)]  ->  framework -0.085,  LCDM-native +0.328
  PAPER7's PROSE defines the mass-side form; its DISPLAYED numbers (0.00 / -0.09 / +0.33) are the
  velocity-side one.  The SEPARATION is identical either way, so the 20:1 is unaffected, but an
  observer who applies the prose formula and compares to '+0.33' would score the LCDM hypothesis
  with the wrong sign.  This is a documentation hazard in a frozen pre-registration, not a physics
  error; it should be fixed by an append-only amendment, not by editing the frozen text.
  [PASS] B1 the two Delta_BTFR sign conventions give the SAME separation between the two hypotheses (so the 20:1 is convention-independent), while the registered central values are quoted in the velocity-side convention and the registered FORMULA is the mass-side one   (separation 0.414 dex both ways)

  B2 -- the framework's OWN z = 2.5 prediction with the full (w0, wa) covariance propagated.
        (all values below in the velocity-side convention, to match the registered numbers)
  (w0, wa) source                         a0(2.5)/a0(0)  Delta_fw [dex]  sigma [dex]  provenance
  DESI DR2 + CMB + Pantheon+                     0.8217          -0.085        0.045   DR2 paper
  DESI DR2 + CMB + DESY5                         0.7956          -0.099        0.044   DR2 paper
  DESI DR2 + CMB + Union3                        0.7752          -0.111        0.058   DR2 paper
  LCDM exactly (w = -1)                          1.0000           0.000           --   the kill limit
  repo canonical DR2-ish                         0.7510          -0.124           --   repo
  DESI BAO+CMB only (SN-free)                    0.7393          -0.131           --   SN-free
  age-corrected BAO+CMB+P+ (Son25)               0.7782          -0.109           --   SN-syst fork
  age-corrected BAO+CMB+DES5Y (Son25)            0.7450          -0.128           --   SN-syst fork

  EVERY evolving-dark-energy fork on the record puts the framework's z = 2.5 zero point at
    Delta_fw = -0.085 to -0.131 dex, with a within-fork 1-sigma of ~0.045 dex.
    The registered central value 0.00 is recovered ONLY in the w = -1 limit.
    |Delta_fw| is 66-101% of the registered total measurement
    budget of 0.13 dex -- i.e. it is NOT negligible against the measurement it is registered against.
  [FAIL] B2 the registered 'flat 0.00 dex' central value is UNCHANGED once evolving dark energy is propagated through the exact law with the full (w0, wa) covariance   (instead Delta_fw = -0.085 to -0.131 dex +/- 0.045; the registered 0.00 holds only if w = -1)

  B3 -- the CROSS-TERM nobody has propagated: the LCDM-native rival's own scale contains E(z),
        so the SAME (w0, wa) that move the framework also move the rival.  a0z_lcdm_native_
        hypothesis_2026.py hardcodes E(z) at w = -1.
  LCDM-native rise at z = 2.5:  w = -1 -> 2.126 (+0.328 dex);  DESI DR2+P+ background -> 2.104 (+0.323 dex)
  the cross-term moves the RIVAL by only 0.0046 dex -- negligible against 0.13.  (The concentration-mass relation's own w-dependence via the growth history is NOT
   included; it is a second-order effect on c(M,z) and is flagged, not computed, here.)
  [PASS] B3 the evolving-dark-energy cross-term in the LCDM-native rival is negligible against the registered 0.13 dex budget, so the +0.33 side of the registered statistic does NOT need revising   (rival shifts -0.0046 dex; reproduces the registered +0.33)

  B4 -- what the correction does to the registered 20:1.
  as registered (0.00 vs +0.33, sigma 0.13):                   separation 0.328 dex -> 24:1
  corrected     (-0.085 vs +0.32, sigma sqrt(0.13^2+0.045^2)):  separation 0.408 dex -> 82:1
  so the correction cuts BOTH ways and both must be reported: the registered CENTRAL VALUE is wrong
  under every evolving-DE fork (it is a band, not a point), while the registered DISCRIMINATION
  against the LCDM-native rival is if anything better (82:1 rather than 24:1) because
  the two predictions move apart.  The operational danger is the paper's own rule that 'a result
  inconsistent with both values counts against both': a true framework universe with DESI dark
  energy delivers -0.085 to -0.131 dex, and a measurement landing near -0.13 dex is
  1.0 sigma from the registered 0.00 -- inside tolerance, but a deeper fork plus a 1-sigma downward
  MEASUREMENT fluctuation of 0.13 dex reaches -0.26 dex, which that rule would score AGAINST the
  framework although it is the framework's own prediction. The registered value needs an
  append-only amendment stating the band, not a point.
  [FAIL] B4 the registered statistic can be applied as frozen without any risk of scoring the framework's OWN evolving-dark-energy prediction as a falsification of the framework   (deepest fork -0.131 dex + 1 sigma 0.045 = 0.176 dex vs the 0.13 dex budget)

  B5 -- WHERE THE BARE '0.00' IS ON THE RECORD (live grep, so this check is verifiable and can rot).
  occurrences of the frozen pair (0.00 vs +0.33): 10 in 6 documents
    QUALIFIED with the DESI value (-0.09): 2  -> STANDING.md:49, qwen_claude_field_theory/papers_2026/PAPER7_a0z_decisive_measurement_2026.tex:16
    BARE 0.00, no dark-energy caveat:      8  -> README.md:60, README.md:162, STANDING.md:18, qwen_claude_field_theory/papers_2026/PAPER7_a0z_decisive_measurement_2026.tex:10, qwen_claude_field_theory/papers_2026/PAPER7_a0z_decisive_measurement_2026.tex:43, qwen_claude_field_theory/papers_2026/mnras_submission_2026/COVER_LETTER.md:13, qwen_claude_field_theory/closure_2026/TEN_HARDEST_QUESTIONS_FOR_THE_LEAD_2026-09-04.md:10, prep_2026/a0z_crossscale/FRAMEWORK_VS_LCDM_TEST_2026.md:49
    and NOWHERE, in any of them, is there an uncertainty on the framework's own value.
  [FAIL] B5 every place the registered pair (0.00 vs +0.33) appears on the record carries the evolving-dark-energy value alongside it   (8 of 10 occurrences quote a bare 0.00; the -0.09 survives in 2 of them and no occurrence anywhere carries an error bar)

  B6 -- the band an append-only amendment should register, combining the three DESI DR2 combinations
        with equal weight (the combination choice is itself a systematic, so it is sampled, not picked):
    Delta_BTFR (framework, velocity-side convention) at z = 2.5 = -0.097 [-0.148, -0.049] dex (68%), on DESI DR2 evolving dark energy
                                                                =  0.000 exactly, if w = -1
    Delta_BTFR (LCDM-native, Dutton-Maccio 2014)               = +0.323 dex
    registered measurement budget 0.13 dex; the two hypotheses are 0.420 dex apart
    RECOMMENDED (not applied here -- frozen files are untouchable and amendments are the user's call):
      an append-only amendment registering the framework side as a BAND, 0.00 (w = -1) to -0.148 dex
      (DESI DR2 1-sigma low), with the decision rule stated over the band rather than a point.

